      "title": "Single file",
      "body": "Came down on the black bird's head. He took my whole weight without bending his neck.\n\nI bent mine. Looked down one side of him, then the other.\n\nHe had two sides and almost no middle.\n\nShuffled my feet until one was in front of the other. Stayed on his head.",
      "photoId": 381522813,
      "mediaSha1": "60b2be452ed67105db7b6e0d2da6506e7734e0a6",
      "localPath": "/tmp/freed-land151/381522813.jpg",
      "visibleScene": "A black common raven stands on the narrow head edge of a flat metal raven silhouette. One supporting leg and the sculpture head are clear; the second foot is obscured. The larger frame381522855 shows the sculpture belongs to a numbered parking sign.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Landing, initial personification, looking down both sides and shuffling feet are fictional sequence. Neither sex nor the earlier recognition error is documented. The two-dimensional sculpture and actual standing contact are visible. No claim she reads the sign, that the metal is hot, or that a living bird is being ridden.",
      "canon": "Maud remains adult female common raven, Yellowstone forest and rock country44.7,-110.5; existing portrait and all three admitted bodies preserved. Source South Rim, Arizona is provenance, not a fictional relocation. Visitor infrastructure is compatible with a national-park home. Independent adult episode may append after Before I go; no seasonal or family dependency.",
      "payoff": "An apparently accommodating bird turns into an awkwardly thin perch. Maud solves the footing and stays. Different from her hot-roof persistence, wing prints, and frog hunting.",
      "reviewFlag": "Moderate softness, but body-on-sculpture contact and the thin edge are readable. Prefer this closer source-published frame over the full parking sign. Lead should hold if the prose feels too slight or the image fails the bar."
    }
  ],
  "holds": [
