      "id": "151-H1",
      "photoId": 109029870,
      "title": "Alongside",
      "body": "He came alongside so close I folded a wing. Dropped below him. He dropped too.\n\nOpened both wings hard. He rose with me.\n\nWe have gone quite a long way without either of us getting out of the other's way.",
      "reason": "HOLD prose: paired flight is real and nicely composed, but this invented mirroring repeats the companion-following pattern without a sufficiently particular consequence. No courtship identification claimed."
    },
    {
      "id": "151-H2",
      "photoId": 415391583,
      "title": "All the way round",
      "body": "Put my foot out and began with the feathers beside it. Followed them up my side.\n\nBy the time I reached my back, I had forgotten where the foot was.\n\nFound it still outside me. Pulled it in before the duck noticed.",
      "reason": "HOLD prose: extended foot and preening juvenile are visible, but weak body-awareness joke ends in audience embarrassment. Do not duplicate Cygnus admitted feather-pulling or underwing-startle scenes."
    }
  ],
